; Tile flags around the entity being updated by #R$B44B
;
; Four scratch bytes written each time #R$B44B samples the tile flag map around an entity (a 16x24 pixel sprite, 2 x 3
; cells) from its position: each is the OR of the flags of two neighbouring cells. #R$B44B then turns them into a mask
; of free directions. The player has its own copy in #R$A89C.
; .
; +0 ProbeRight: the two cells to the right of the sprite (rows 1 and 2)
; +1 ProbeLeft: the two cells to the left (rows 1 and 2)
; +2 ProbeBelow: the two cells under the feet
; +3 ProbeHead: the two cells of the top row of the sprite
@label=ProbeRight
g$8559 DEFB $00
@label=ProbeLeft
 $855A DEFB $00
@label=ProbeBelow
 $855B DEFB $00
@label=ProbeHead
 $855C DEFB $00
